[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3316210571","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110757#issuecomment-3316210571","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110757","id":3316210571,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7FqVuL","user":{"login":"MajorMcDoom","id":13228932,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzMjI4OTMy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13228932?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom","html_url":"https://github.com/MajorMcDoom","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-21T19:24:47Z","updated_at":"2025-09-21T19:24:47Z","body":"Tagging @mihe in case it rings a bell.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3316210571/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3318597774","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110757#issuecomment-3318597774","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110757","id":3318597774,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7FzciO","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-22T12:09:00Z","updated_at":"2025-09-22T16:49:21Z","body":"> error only occurs during collisions\n> [...]\n> setting `max_contacts_reported` to `0` makes the error go away\n> [...]\n> using the old Godot physics makes the error go away\n\nThat means it can only be one or both of these calls:\n\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/149a4b4ca12e2baf700020fc10f00d5b0a5e9f0d/modules/jolt_physics/spaces/jolt_contact_listener_3d.cpp#L198-L199\n\nThe only possible explanation that I can see, since we always `clear()` those contact lists after every physics step, is that either `JPH::ContactListener::OnContactAdded` and `JPH::ContactListener::OnContactPersisted` are both being called for the same sub-shape pair in a single step, or one of those two callbacks is being called multiple times for the same sub-shape pair.\n\nIs that a thing that can/should happen @jrouwe? I was under the impression that only one of them would be called per step and per sub-shape pair, and only once.\n\n@MajorMcDoom If you're able/willing, just removing those two `reserve` calls should work as a quick test to see if they're the culprit.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3318597774/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3320125980","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110757#issuecomment-3320125980","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110757","id":3320125980,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7F5Roc","user":{"login":"MajorMcDoom","id":13228932,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzMjI4OTMy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13228932?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom","html_url":"https://github.com/MajorMcDoom","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-22T16:43:17Z","updated_at":"2025-09-22T16:43:26Z","body":">  [@MajorMcDoom](https://github.com/MajorMcDoom) If you're able/willing, just removing those two `reserve` calls should work as a quick test to see if they're the culprit.\n\nSure thing, I will do that test some time today!\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3320125980/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3320461145","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110757#issuecomment-3320461145","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110757","id":3320461145,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7F6jdZ","user":{"login":"MajorMcDoom","id":13228932,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzMjI4OTMy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13228932?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom","html_url":"https://github.com/MajorMcDoom","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-22T17:45:57Z","updated_at":"2025-09-22T17:45:57Z","body":"@mihe Confirmed, commenting out those two lines made the errors go away.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3320461145/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3320647396","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110757#issuecomment-3320647396","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110757","id":3320647396,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7F7Q7k","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-22T18:18:58Z","updated_at":"2025-09-22T18:30:26Z","body":"> [@mihe](https://github.com/mihe) Confirmed, commenting out those two lines made the errors go away.\n\nGreat, thank you for confirming, then my questions above still stand.\n\nIf anyone is wondering why this started appearing in 4.5, this particular error was introduced to `LocalVector::reserve` in #105278, in order to make things consistent across the different collections in Godot, which already had similar checks for catching mistakes when reserving capacity. I guess that ended up being helpful here.\n\nEDIT: It's probably also worth mentioning that if the `OnContactAdded`/`OnContactPersisted` callbacks can be called multiple times for the same sub-shape pairs, then there would be thread-safety concerns if those multiple calls can happen concurrently, since these particular lists aren't thread-safe.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3320647396/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3321371154","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110757#issuecomment-3321371154","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110757","id":3321371154,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7F-BoS","user":{"login":"jrouwe","id":1621693,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjE2OTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1621693?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe","html_url":"https://github.com/jrouwe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-22T20:25:27Z","updated_at":"2025-09-22T20:25:27Z","body":"> Is that a thing that can/should happen @jrouwe? I was under the impression that only one of them would be called per step and per sub-shape pair, and only once.\n\nI don't think that should be possible unless you call `PhysicsSystem::Update` with multiple collision steps (which you don't). The only edge case that I can think of is that a body collides both in the discrete and in the continuous collision detection stage, but that should technically not be possible (although `setting continuous_cd to false makes the error go away` suggests that it could be the reason).","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3321371154/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3321506473","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110757#issuecomment-3321506473","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110757","id":3321506473,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7F-iqp","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-22T21:12:22Z","updated_at":"2025-09-22T21:13:27Z","body":"> The only edge case that I can think of is that a body collides both in the discrete and in the continuous collision detection stage, but that should technically not be possible (although `setting continuous_cd to false makes the error go away` suggests that it could be the reason).\n\nSeeing as how @MajorMcDoom likely won't be able to produce a minimal repro project for this, is there maybe some logging they could add somewhere (as a one-off test) to confirm whether or not this is what's happening?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3321506473/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3325401985","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110757#issuecomment-3325401985","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110757","id":3325401985,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7GNZuB","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-23T20:17:32Z","updated_at":"2025-09-23T20:17:32Z","body":"Hi, FYI, the message has been moved to verbose logging on latest `master` (soon to be cherry-picked to 4.5) since https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110826.\nIf you plan to investigate this after then, please remember to turn on verbose logging.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3325401985/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3325560625","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110757#issuecomment-3325560625","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110757","id":3325560625,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7GOAcx","user":{"login":"MajorMcDoom","id":13228932,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzMjI4OTMy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13228932?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom","html_url":"https://github.com/MajorMcDoom","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-23T21:09:27Z","updated_at":"2025-09-23T21:09:27Z","body":"For now, can someone tell me if this error is harmless, or if it is reflective of something really bad happening that I shouldn't ignore?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3325560625/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3325571559","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110757#issuecomment-3325571559","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110757","id":3325571559,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7GODHn","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-23T21:13:05Z","updated_at":"2025-09-23T22:35:30Z","body":"~Don't worry about it. The message just indicates that something odd is happening.~\n~I do recommend to investigators to track it down, but most likely it just results in a negligible inefficiency.~\nEdit: Seems like this one is more serious, see below.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3325571559/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3325626826","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110757#issuecomment-3325626826","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110757","id":3325626826,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7GOQnK","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-23T21:34:03Z","updated_at":"2025-09-23T21:34:03Z","body":"> For now, can someone tell me if this error is harmless, or if it is reflective of something really bad happening that I shouldn't ignore?\n\nIt depends on what's actually happening, but I wouldn't call it harmless. In the worst case you have a race condition and potential crash/corruption/whatever, and in the best case the list of contacts for the affected bodies will have a bunch of extraneous (duplicate?) contacts in it. The contact depth will also be overwritten by whatever the last call to those callbacks is, which may or may not be problematic I guess.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3325626826/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3325724407","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110757#issuecomment-3325724407","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110757","id":3325724407,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7GOob3","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-23T22:18:59Z","updated_at":"2025-09-23T22:18:59Z","body":"I put up a pull request (#110844) to make a more \"official\" error out of this. This will effectively resurface the error that was put behind the `--verbose` flag as of #110826, albeit with a different error message.\n\nIt should also stop the potentially multiple contact manifolds from being merged, unlike the current `reserve()` error, but it won't help if there's some race condition happening.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3325724407/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3325964822","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110757#issuecomment-3325964822","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110757","id":3325964822,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7GPjIW","user":{"login":"MajorMcDoom","id":13228932,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzMjI4OTMy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13228932?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom","html_url":"https://github.com/MajorMcDoom","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-24T00:14:55Z","updated_at":"2025-09-24T00:14:55Z","body":"> I put up a pull request ([#110844](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110844)) to make a more \"official\" error out of this. This will effectively resurface the error that was put behind the `--verbose` flag as of [#110826](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110826), albeit with a different error message.\n> \n> It should also stop the potentially multiple contact manifolds from being merged, unlike the current `reserve()` error, but it won't help if there's some race condition happening.\n\nCan a race condition happen even if I don't have the physics set to run on a separate thread?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3325964822/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3327841320","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110757#issuecomment-3327841320","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110757","id":3327841320,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7GWtQo","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-24T11:10:53Z","updated_at":"2025-09-24T11:56:10Z","body":"> Can a race condition happen even if I don't have the physics set to run on a separate thread?\n\nYes. Both the Jolt integration and Godot Physics will always use as many threads as are available through `WorkerThreadPool` during the physics step, even when the \"Run on Separate Thread\" setting is disabled, and those worker threads are what's at play here. That setting just allows the main thread to not be blocked while the physics engine is being stepped.\n\nBut again, that's assuming the worst possible case. I get the sense that the CCD stuff happens at a completely separate (later?) stage, so a collision being reported in both the discrete and CCD stages might not risk overlapping at all, meaning there wouldn't be any race condition.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3327841320/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3330545749","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110757#issuecomment-3330545749","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110757","id":3330545749,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7GhBhV","user":{"login":"jrouwe","id":1621693,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjE2OTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1621693?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe","html_url":"https://github.com/jrouwe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-24T20:16:34Z","updated_at":"2025-09-24T20:16:34Z","body":"Discrete and CCD don't overlap in time and 1 body pair is handled by 1 thread only:\n\n<img width=\"2207\" height=\"718\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2c182934-5571-4daa-b485-022582380b80\" />\n\nLooking at the code, I think the issue is that a contact is found in both the discrete and CCD step (I thought I had a check to prevent that, but I can't find it right now). It would require very specific conditions to trigger:\n\n* The body A would need to use CCD and be overlapping with B at the beginning of the time step\n* Other bodies need to be involved so that the penetration between A and B is not resolved at the end of the discrete step\n* A still needs to be moving towards B with significant enough velocity to trigger CCD after the discrete step\n\nI haven't been able to repro this in a test bed.\n\nIn any case I don't think there's a race condition.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3330545749/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3333895851","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110757#issuecomment-3333895851","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110757","id":3333895851,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Gtzar","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-25T13:06:35Z","updated_at":"2025-09-25T13:06:35Z","body":"> In any case I don't think there's a race condition.\n\nGlad to hear it.\n\n> I thought I had a check to prevent that, but I can't find it right now\n\nForgive the naive question, but assuming you can't find this existing check, would it be possible to just add one?\n\nAlso, just to clarify, #110844 wasn't meant to be the logging I asked about [above](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110757#issuecomment-3321506473). I was thinking more along the lines of a patch that @MajorMcDoom could apply locally to Jolt itself to help confirm what's happening exactly, if that makes any sense.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3333895851/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3335619122","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110757#issuecomment-3335619122","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110757","id":3335619122,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7G0YIy","user":{"login":"jrouwe","id":1621693,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjE2OTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1621693?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe","html_url":"https://github.com/jrouwe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-25T19:23:02Z","updated_at":"2025-09-25T19:23:02Z","body":"I've done some further debugging and it is indeed possible to get contact callbacks for the same shape pair in the same step. I really had to engineer a situation in the Jolt Samples app to trigger this (stepping through the code and each time it took an early out changing the sample to bypass that early out):\n\n[ContactListenerTest.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/22546218/ContactListenerTest.zip)\n\nI've got 4 boxes: \n\n<img width=\"1056\" height=\"416\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c434106c-79df-4e1a-92e8-9ba56d83d0ed\" />\n\nThe bodies are all initially overlapping (because of `Speculative Contact Distance`) and I had to set the `Continuous CD Movement Treshold` to 0 to ensure that CCD is always performed (not recommended).\n\n<img width=\"1203\" height=\"733\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4356c868-ee1b-481a-bb13-665530aa1f25\" />\n\nB has high speed towards C but is blocked from going back by A. B is blocked from moving forward by D.\n\nThis results in:\n\n```\nOnContactAdded A B\nOnContactAdded C D\nOnContactAdded B C\nOnContactPersisted B C\n```\n\nIn other words you get an `OnContactAdded` followed by a `OnContactPersisted` for B and C in the same step. As said before, they happen in different jobs, so there is no race condition.\n\nPast Jorrit was kind enough to document for future Jorrit (who had forgotten about this) why this is. First we check if we already created a contact this step:\n\nhttps://github.com/jrouwe/JoltPhysics/blob/589106a4928f7fba92f2333081a0caf8d2447113/Jolt/Physics/Constraints/ContactConstraintManager.cpp#L1384-L1387\n\nFollowed by a call to `OnContactPersisted` because otherwise we cannot obtain the contact settings (which would mean we don't know what e.g. the restitution is):\n\nhttps://github.com/jrouwe/JoltPhysics/blob/589106a4928f7fba92f2333081a0caf8d2447113/Jolt/Physics/Constraints/ContactConstraintManager.cpp#L1417-L1419\n\nThere would be the option to completely ignore any CCD collisions if bodies already collided in the discrete step, but that would allow bodies tunneling through other bodies which is not what we want.\n\nSo, I think the solution now is to handle this on the godot side. Best is probably to only store the contact manifold on 1st contact as the bodies still have their original velocities at that point. Any subsequent contacts should return the proper collision settings but can be ignored for the purpose of storing the manifold.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3335619122/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3336232552","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110757#issuecomment-3336232552","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110757","id":3336232552,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7G2t5o","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-25T23:30:45Z","updated_at":"2025-09-25T23:30:45Z","body":"> I really had to engineer a situation in the Jolt Samples app to trigger this (stepping through the code and each time it took an early out changing the sample to bypass that early out)\n\nI appreciate the effort! I replicated your test in Godot and can confirm that it causes the `reserve() called with a capacity smaller than the current size.` error in 4.5-stable: [jolt-contact-error.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/22549329/jolt-contact-error.zip)\n\n> So, I think the solution now is to handle this on the godot side. Best is probably to only store the contact manifold on 1st contact as the bodies still have their original velocities at that point. Any subsequent contacts should return the proper collision settings but can be ignored for the purpose of storing the manifold.\n\nI've put up a new pull request that should hopefully do what you describe: #110914","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3336232552/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3336366989","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110757#issuecomment-3336366989","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110757","id":3336366989,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7G3OuN","user":{"login":"MajorMcDoom","id":13228932,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzMjI4OTMy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13228932?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom","html_url":"https://github.com/MajorMcDoom","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-26T00:35:45Z","updated_at":"2025-09-26T00:35:45Z","body":"Thank you for looking into this! 🙏","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3336366989/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]